## 3. Statistical Data Profiling

### What is Data Profiling?

**Data Profiling** analyzes data to understand its structure, content, and quality.

### MaritimeIQ Implementation

```csharp
public class DataProfiler
{
    public DataProfile ProfileData(DataFrame df)
    {
        return new DataProfile
        {
            RowCount = df.Count(),
            ColumnCount = df.Columns.Length,
            NullCounts = CalculateNullCounts(df),
            DistinctCounts = CalculateDistinctCounts(df),
            Statistics = CalculateStatistics(df),
            DataTypes = GetDataTypes(df)
        };
    }
    
    private Dictionary<string, ColumnStatistics> CalculateStatistics(DataFrame df)
    {
        var stats = new Dictionary<string, ColumnStatistics>();
        
        foreach (var column in df.Columns)
        {
            if (IsNumeric(column))
            {
                stats[column] = new ColumnStatistics
                {
                    Min = df.Aggregate(min(column)).First()[column],
                    Max = df.Aggregate(max(column)).First()[column],
                    Mean = df.Aggregate(avg(column)).First()[column],
                    StdDev = CalculateStandardDeviation(df, column),
                    Percentiles = CalculatePercentiles(df, column)
                };
            }
        }
        
        return stats;
    }
}
```

**Benefits**:
- Understand data distribution
- Identify outliers
- Detect data quality issues
- Guide data cleaning

