## 5. Data Drift Detection

### What is Data Drift?

**Data Drift** occurs when the statistical properties of data change over time.

### MaritimeIQ Implementation

```csharp
public class DataDriftDetector
{
    public DriftResult DetectDrift(DataFrame baseline, DataFrame current, string column)
    {
        var baselineStats = CalculateStatistics(baseline, column);
        var currentStats = CalculateStatistics(current, column);
        
        var driftScore = CalculateDriftScore(baselineStats, currentStats);
        
        return new DriftResult
        {
            Column = column,
            BaselineMean = baselineStats.Mean,
            CurrentMean = currentStats.Mean,
            BaselineStdDev = baselineStats.StdDev,
            CurrentStdDev = currentStats.StdDev,
            DriftScore = driftScore,
            IsDrifted = driftScore > 0.1 // 10% threshold
        };
    }
    
    private double CalculateDriftScore(Statistics baseline, Statistics current)
    {
        var meanDrift = Math.Abs(baseline.Mean - current.Mean) / baseline.Mean;
        var stdDevDrift = Math.Abs(baseline.StdDev - current.StdDev) / baseline.StdDev;
        
        return (meanDrift + stdDevDrift) / 2;
    }
}
```

**Benefits**:
- Early detection of data changes
- ML model performance monitoring
- Data quality degradation alerts
- Proactive remediation

